# ⭐ Re-ranking

Vector Search retrieves many candidate documents.

Example:

```
50 Documents
```

Not all are equally relevant.

Re-ranking sorts them again.

```
Vector Search

↓

50 Documents

↓

Re-ranker

↓

Top 5 Documents
```

---

# Why Re-ranking is Needed

Similarity Search uses vector distance.

Two documents may have similar scores.

The Re-ranker performs a deeper comparison to determine which documents best answer the question.

---

# 🧠 Cross Encoder

The most common production re-ranking model.

Instead of comparing embeddings independently,

it processes:

```
Question

+

Document
```

together.

Example:

Question

```
What is Dependency Injection?
```

Document A

```
FastAPI Dependency Injection
```

Document B

```
Python Variables
```

Cross Encoder assigns a higher score to Document A.

---

# Bi-Encoder vs Cross Encoder

| Bi-Encoder | Cross Encoder |
|------------|---------------|
| Generates Embeddings | Re-ranks Results |
| Fast | Slower |
| Independent Encoding | Joint Encoding |
| Good Recall | Excellent Precision |

---

# 🔝 Top-K Retrieval

Similarity Search may retrieve:

```
100 Documents
```

After Re-ranking,

Top-K selects:

```
Top 5
```

Only these are sent to the LLM.

Benefits:

- Lower Token Usage
- Faster Responses
- Better Accuracy

---

# 🗜 Context Compression

Sometimes Top-5 documents are still too large.

Instead of sending everything,

the system extracts only relevant paragraphs.

Original:

```
20 Pages
```

Compressed:

```
Relevant 3 Paragraphs
```

Benefits:

- Lower Token Cost
- Faster Inference
- Less Noise
- Better Responses

