# 💬 Common Interview Questions

## Why Hybrid Search?

Because Vector Search may miss exact keywords while BM25 may miss semantic meaning.

Combining both provides better retrieval.

---

## Why Re-ranking?

Similarity Search retrieves candidates.

Re-ranking determines which candidates are actually the most relevant.

---

## Why Top-K?

To reduce token usage and avoid sending unnecessary context.

---

## Why Context Compression?

Large context windows increase latency and cost.

Compression keeps only important information.

---

## Why Query Rewriting?

Users often ask incomplete or ambiguous questions.

Rewriting improves retrieval quality.

---

## Why Multi-Query Retrieval?

Different wording retrieves different documents.

Multiple queries improve recall.

---

# ❌ Common Mistakes

### Mistake 1

❌ Vector Search alone is enough.

✔ Production systems combine Vector Search, BM25, Metadata Filtering, and Re-ranking.

---

### Mistake 2

❌ Highest similarity score always gives the best answer.

✔ Similarity Search is only the first stage.

Re-ranking improves precision.

---

### Mistake 3

❌ Send every retrieved document to the LLM.

✔ Only send the highest-ranked and most relevant context.

