# ⚡ 30-Second Interview Answer

> In production RAG systems, retrieval involves much more than vector search. We first understand and rewrite the user's query, apply metadata filters, perform Hybrid Search using BM25 and Vector Search, merge the results, re-rank them using a Cross Encoder, select the Top-K documents, compress the context if necessary, and finally send an optimized prompt to the LLM. This pipeline improves retrieval accuracy, reduces hallucinations, lowers latency, and minimizes token costs.

