# 📌 Production Best Practices

✅ Combine Vector Search with BM25 using Hybrid Search.

✅ Always apply metadata filtering before retrieval.

✅ Rewrite ambiguous user queries.

✅ Use Multi-Query Retrieval for complex questions.

✅ Re-rank retrieved documents before passing them to the LLM.

✅ Limit context using Top-K.

✅ Compress large contexts before prompt creation.

✅ Continuously evaluate retrieval quality using real production queries.

---

# 🎯 Key Takeaways

- Retrieval is the heart of every RAG system.
- Hybrid Search combines semantic and keyword search.
- BM25 is excellent for exact keywords, IDs, and codes.
- Metadata Filtering improves accuracy, speed, and security.
- Query Rewriting improves retrieval for vague user questions.
- Multi-Query Retrieval increases document recall.
- Re-ranking improves precision after initial retrieval.
- Cross Encoders are commonly used for production re-ranking.
- Top-K limits the amount of context sent to the LLM.
- Context Compression reduces token usage while preserving important information.
- Production RAG systems combine all of these techniques to deliver accurate, fast, and cost-effective responses.

